BT /F1 14 Tf 50 720 Td (Tomato Disease Prevention and Management) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 690 Td (Tomato \(Solanum lycopersicum\) is prone to various fungal and bacterial infections.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 672 Td (Common Diseases:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 654 Td (1. Early Blight \(Alternaria solani\): Brown circular spots with concentric rings on leaves.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 636 Td (   Management: Space plants well for airflow. Apply copper-based fungicides or chlorothalonil.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 618 Td (2. Late Blight \(Phytophthora infestans\): Rapid water-soaked dark lesions on foliage and fruit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 600 Td (   Management: Avoid overhead irrigation, remove infected plants immediately.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 582 Td (3. Fusarium Wilt: Yellowing of lower leaves progressing upwards.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 564 Td (   Management: Use resistant varieties and practice crop rotation with non-solanaceous crops.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 546 Td (General Prevention Practices:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 528 Td (Maintain proper soil drainage, practice drip irrigation, and mulch the soil to prevent spore splash.) Tj ET

